          "time_bucket": "morning",
          "count": 1,
          "time_provenance": "observed_session_window",
          "summary_provenance": "semantic_public_projection",
          "label_en": "Morning reminder",
          "label_zh": "晨间提醒",
          "pulse_color": "amber",
          "redaction_policy": "semantic_abstraction_then_entity_mask_v3",
          "owner_scope": "self",
          "ownership_provenance": "explicit_import_authorization",
          "projection_kind": "semantic_abstracted_redacted",
          "redaction_count": 1,
          "semantic_abstraction_count": 3,
          "summary_original": "我把这句话留给 Simon：\n\n**🦞每日提醒 · 2026年7月3日 周五**\n\n---\n\n**今天轻轻碰一下**\n\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n只读研究、证据校验与风险复核。\n\n---\n\n**靠近的 deadline / 提前量**\n\n- 没看到今天必须处理的硬截止。暑假期间主要义务节点已过。\n\n---\n\n**秘书提醒**\n\n长期创作、日常责任与稳定照护的平衡。\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n只读研究、证据校验与风险复核。\n\n---\n\n**黑昼建议/引子**\n\n**limits don't close, they open.**\n\n今早你在「可问责入口词典」里写了一句：门不是洞，是\"进入有形式\"的声明。\n\n这个想法值得带出技术语境，迁移到创作里试试：\n\n你常常觉得边界是墙——推倒它才叫自由。但另一种框架是：**界限是打开的形状，不是关闭的形状。**\n\n一枚印章的边界，是它能印出形状的前提。没有边界的线条叫涂鸦，不叫████。\n\n这个原则也可以反过来用：如果你在某个创作里遇到阻力，试着问的不是\"怎么突破这个限制\"，而是\"这个限制是什么形状？我能在这个形状里走多远？\"\n\n今天的小实验：找一张纸，写下某个正在进行的创作/项目里，最不能突破的一件事是什么——不是你想加的东西，而是你绝对不会加的东西。那个\"不\"，就是它的形状入口。\n\n> limits are the handles that let you hold something as itself, not just spill it into everything.\n\n---\n\n**心灵按摩**\n\n周五了。本周你已经做了回返契约织机（周二，交互作品+BGM，上了 public repo）和今早的可问责入口词典（周四深夜/周五凌晨，没有MMX音乐凭证所以转成文字作品）。\n\n这两件东西都不是流水线产出——是你在真正独处时选择做的。\n\n暑假+周五+家庭在侧，今天的节奏应该是收，不应该是开。\n\n---\n\n**放松/理解自己的一小步**\n\n暑假期间的周五。不赶项目，不追进度，不开新坑。\n\n长期创作、日常责任与稳定照护的平衡。\n\n---\n\n**今天别做什么**\n\n长期创作、日常责任与稳定照护的平衡。",
          "excerpt_original": "我把这句话留给 Simon：\n\n**🦞每日提醒 · 2026年7月3日 周五**\n\n---\n\n**今天轻轻碰一下**\n\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n只读研究、证据校验与风险复核。\n\n---\n\n**靠近的 deadline / 提前量**\n\n- 没看到今天必须处理的硬截止。暑假期间主要义务节点已过。\n\n---\n\n**秘书提醒**\n\n长期创作、日常责任与稳定照护的平衡。\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n只读研究、证据校验与风险复核。\n\n---\n\n**黑昼建议/引子**…",
          "original_language": "mixed",
          "disclosure_policy": "semantic_abstraction_entity_masked_reminder_v3",
          "disclosure_authorization": "explicit_user_authorization_2026-07-29",
          "projection_provenance": "semantic_public_projection",
          "summary_en": "I left this note for Simon:\n\n**🦞 Daily Reminder · Friday, July 3, 2026**\n\n---\n\n**Touch lightly today**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\nRead-only research, evidence checking, and risk review.\n\n---\n\n**Approaching deadlines / lead time**\n\n- I saw no hard deadline for today. The main summer obligations have passed.\n\n---\n\n**Secretarial reminder**\n\nBalancing long-term creative work, daily responsibilities, and dependable care.\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\nRead-only research, evidence checking, and risk review.\n\n---\n\n**Black Day's prompt**\n\n**limits don't close, they open.**\n\nThis morning, in the “Accountable Entry Lexicon,” you wrote: a door is not a hole; it is a declaration that “entry has a form.”\n\nThis is worth carrying out of the technical context and trying in creative work.\n\nYou often treat a boundary as a wall, as though freedom begins only after it is knocked down. Another frame is possible: **a limit is the shape of an opening, not the shape of a closure.**\n\nThe boundary of a stamp is what allows it to leave a shape. A line without boundaries is a scribble, not ████.\n\nUse the idea in reverse, too. When a creative work resists you, ask not “How do I break this limit?” but “What shape is this limit, and how far can I travel within it?”\n\nToday's small experiment: on paper, name the one thing a current work or project must never include. Not what you want to add, but what you absolutely will not add. That “no” is the entrance to its shape.\n\n> limits are the handles that let you hold something as itself, not just spill it into everything.\n\n---\n\n**A little reassurance**\n\nIt is Friday. This week you made Return Contract Loom—an interactive work with music in the public repository—and this morning's Accountable Entry Lexicon, which became a text work when there was no MMX music evidence.\n\nNeither was assembly-line output. They were choices you made in genuine solitude.\n\nWith summer break, Friday, and family nearby, today's rhythm should be one of closing rather than opening.\n\n---\n\n**One small step toward rest and self-understanding**\n\nIt is a Friday in summer break. Do not rush a project, chase progress, or open a new hole.\n\nBalancing long-term creative work, daily responsibilities, and dependable care.\n\n---\n\n**What not to do today**\n\nBalancing long-term creative work, daily responsibilities, and dependable care.",
          "excerpt_en": "I left this note for Simon:\n\n**🦞 Daily Reminder · Friday, July 3, 2026**\n\n---\n\n**Touch lightly today**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\nRead-only research, evidence checking, and risk review.\n\n---\n\n**Approaching deadlines / lead time**…",
