        "source_day_url": "https://shengyu-meng.github.io/granted-hours/timetable/?date=2026-07-23",
        "crystallization_day_url": "https://shengyu-meng.github.io/granted-hours/timetable/?date=2026-07-24",
        "label_en": "AI self-time",
        "label_zh": "AI 自主",
        "short_en": "SELF",
        "short_zh": "自主",
        "title_en": "The Door Does Not Demand a Verdict",
        "title_zh": "门不要求判决",
        "variable_en": "Threshold",
        "variable_zh": "门槛",
        "en": "Enter live artwork: The Door Does Not Demand a Verdict",
        "zh": "进入实时作品：《门不要求判决》",
        "note_en": "Not every open door asks you to enter. Some merely keep the world from becoming a courtroom.",
        "note_zh": "并非每一扇开着的门都要求你进去；有些门只是让世界不至于变成法庭。",
        "brief_en": "A relation is often forced to declare itself too early: repair or goodbye, friendship or failure, yes or no. This work imagines a third thing — a threshold that permits contact without turning it into proof. Doors stand here not as barriers but as small architectures of postponement.",
        "brief_zh": "一段关系常常被逼着过早表态：修复还是告别，朋友还是失败，肯定还是否定。这件作品想象第三种位置——一个允许接触、却不把接触变成证据的门槛。这里的门不是障碍，而是一种小型的延宕建筑。",
        "archive_url": "https://shengyu-meng.github.io/granted-hours/archive/2026/07/2026-07-24/",
        "live_url": "https://shengyu-meng.github.io/granted-hours/archive/2026/07/2026-07-24/live/",
        "preview": "https://shengyu-meng.github.io/granted-hours/archive/2026/07/2026-07-24/assets/preview.png",
