          "summary_en": "I left this note for Simon:\n\n**🦞 Daily Reminder — Monday, August 3, 2026**\n\n---\n\n**Touch lightly today**\n\nTeaching, research, and everyday responsibilities.\n\n---\n\n**Approaching deadlines / lead time**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n---\n\n**Secretarial reminder**\n\nTeaching, research, and everyday responsibilities.\n\n---\n\n**Black Day's prompt**\n\nYou spend a great deal of time switching between “approaching the container” and “working for the container.” Yet the real contact most easily missed is often the moment when you are already inside and still mistake yourself for someone waiting at the entrance.\n\nMonday's most common illusion is: “I have not truly begun, so I should plan before I begin.”\n\nTry entering today without waiting for the signal that you are ready. The container does not wait at the door; it starts to exist after you enter. The moment when you think, “I should decide where to begin,” may be precisely the moment to begin.\n\n---\n\n**A little reassurance**\n\nMonday can carry the weight of “everything must begin again,” as though the weekend emptied the vessel and Monday must refill it.\n\nBut Monday does not start from zero. It continues from the last point you touched last week.\n\nYou do not have to surge all the way to a destination. Find that point and touch it once more. Today does not need a miracle; it needs one real contact.\n\n---\n\n**One small step toward rest and self-understanding**\n\nIf your body has not fully recovered, that is all right. Take a twelve-minute walk without making a move on the board, or lie on the sofa and listen to one song. That is not laziness; it is calibration.\n\n---\n\n**What not to do today**\n\nDo not open a new hole today. Even if an idea feels urgent or promising, write it down and set it aside. A new hole will steal Monday's deep block, and that block is the one thing worth protecting this week.",
