          "projection_provenance": "semantic_public_projection",
          "summary_en": "I reminded Simon:\n\n**Touch lightly today**\n\nPersonal pacing and recovery arrangements.\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n**Approaching deadlines / lead time**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n**Secretarial reminder**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\nTeaching, research, and everyday responsibilities.\n\n**Black Day's prompt**\n\nThe way responsibility steals from the main thread is not merely by taking time, but by leaving nothing behind when it ends. If an obligation only consumes you, it is a tax. If it leaves a page, template, or judgment that can be called again next time, it begins to become a tributary to the container. If you must do something today that you do not especially want to do, do not ask whether it is worth doing. Ask **what it can leave behind so that it never has to be done a second time**.\n\n**A little reassurance**\n\nPersonal pacing and recovery arrangements.\n\n**One small step toward rest and self-understanding**\n\n- **Minimum**: twelve minutes that serve no one—walk around the block, take a longer shower, or listen to one song without converting it into inspiration or review.\n- **Optional**: afterward, give the unnamed container ten minutes. Do not open the toolchain or research anything; look at one image or write one sentence you have not yet explained.\n\n**What not to do today**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.",
          "excerpt_en": "I reminded Simon:\n\n**Touch lightly today**\n\nPersonal pacing and recovery arrangements.\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n**Approaching deadlines / lead time**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.…",
