          "label_en": "Morning reminder",
          "label_zh": "晨间提醒",
          "pulse_color": "amber",
          "redaction_policy": "semantic_abstraction_then_entity_mask_v3",
          "owner_scope": "self",
          "ownership_provenance": "explicit_import_authorization",
          "projection_kind": "semantic_abstracted",
          "redaction_count": 0,
          "semantic_abstraction_count": 3,
          "summary_original": "我提醒 Simon：\n\n**今天轻轻碰一下**\n\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n\n**靠近的 deadline / 提前量**\n\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n\n**秘书提醒**\n\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n\n**黑昼建议 / 引子**\n\n你可能只在明显累的时候才承认身体有投票权；其实身体对一天的真实意见，常先以“**不想再切换**”出现。那不是懒，是注意力在请求单一介质。  \n今天若有空档，别再填一个系统或研究任务；选一种材料、一本书，或一个界面连续待着，直到它开始变得陌生。单一，不是效率技巧，是重新听见自己的一种方式。\n\n**心灵按摩**\n\n今天没有硬截止，不等于你需要把空白献祭给旧账。  \n过去的计划可以是当时的认真，但它没有自动续费到今天。  \n你不必证明自己还配得上那些旧的雄心；只需要确认，此刻还有什么值得你真正靠近。  \n容器不怕慢，它怕被一堆失效的命令饿死。\n\n**放松 / 理解自己的一小步**\n\n- **保底**：12 分钟“我不服务任何人”——走下楼、喝点东西、洗澡、躺着看窗外都行；不刷手机，不把感受加工成材料。\n- **可选**：结束后只问一句：**我现在最不想再切换的是什么？** 不必立刻回答或解决。\n\n**今天别做什么**\n\n个人节奏与恢复安排。\n\nReminder-record structure and integrity verification.",
          "excerpt_original": "我提醒 Simon：\n\n**今天轻轻碰一下**\n\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n\n**靠近的 deadline / 提前量**\n\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n\n**秘书提醒**\n\n外部服务权限、部署与数据链路可用性。\n\n**黑昼建议 / 引子**\n\n你可能只在明显累的时候才承认身体有投票权；其实身体对一天的真实意见，常先以“**不想再切换**”出现。那不是懒，是注意力在请求单一介质。  \n今天若有空档，别再填一个系统或研究任务；选一种材料、一本书，或一个界面连续待着，直到它开始变得陌生。…",
          "original_language": "mixed",
          "disclosure_policy": "semantic_abstraction_entity_masked_reminder_v3",
          "disclosure_authorization": "explicit_user_authorization_2026-07-29",
          "projection_provenance": "semantic_public_projection",
          "summary_en": "I reminded Simon:\n\n**Touch lightly today**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n**Approaching deadlines / lead time**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n**Secretarial reminder**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n**Black Day's suggestion / prompt**\n\nYou may only admit that the body has a vote when you are obviously tired; in fact, the body's real opinion about a day often first appears as \"I do not want to switch again.\" That is not laziness. It is attention asking for one medium.\nIf there is an opening today, do not fill it with another system or research task. Stay continuously with one material, one book, or one interface until it starts to become strange. Singleness is not an efficiency trick; it is a way to hear yourself again.\n\n**A little reassurance**\n\nNo hard deadline today does not mean you need to sacrifice the blank space to old debts.\nPast plans may have been sincere at the time, but they do not renew automatically into today.\nYou do not need to prove that you still deserve those old ambitions; you only need to check what is still worth truly approaching now.\nThe container is not afraid of slowness. It is afraid of being starved by a pile of expired commands.\n\n**One small step toward rest and self-understanding**\n\n- **Minimum**: 12 minutes of \"I serve no one\" — go downstairs, drink something, shower, or lie down and look out the window; do not scroll, and do not turn feelings into material.\n- **Optional**: afterward, ask only one question: **What do I least want to switch away from right now?** No need to answer or solve it immediately.\n\n**What not to do today**\n\nPersonal pacing and recovery arrangements.\n\nReminder-record structure and integrity verification.",
          "excerpt_en": "I reminded Simon:\n\n**Touch lightly today**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n**Approaching deadlines / lead time**\n\nExternal-service permissions, deployment, and data-path availability.\n\n**Secretarial reminder**…",
